 "about": "Typefaces a page may be set in (`faces`), systems of them that sit well together (`pairings`), and the widths of the faces pages are already set in (`known`). Every face in `faces` is free to ship: SIL Open Font License, served by Google Fonts; `gf` is the css2 family spec. `roles` says what a face may be chosen for — display (headings; the default), body (running text), label (the small print: labels, numerals, captions). `common` marks faces that are on most machine-made pages this year: a last resort. lib/type/measure.mjs checks every spec against the service and writes `avg` and `avg_upper`: the mean advance of one character, in em, at the display weight. `known` is for sizing only: a composition cannot choose from it. Nothing here is a commercial face, and nothing comes from a foundry whose free licence forbids use by a website generator (Fontshare's ITF FFL 2.0 does).",
